# Egregore pytest batches

When running or verifying tests in `projects/egregore/`, **always use batch mode** — do not run `uv run pytest` on the entire `tests/` tree in one process.

## Command

From `projects/egregore/`:

```bash
./scripts/pytest_batches.sh                              # full suite — pre-PR / cross-cutting changes
./scripts/pytest_batches.sh tests/domain tests/application  # targeted — after a focused change
./scripts/pytest_batches.sh tests/domain -- -k run_context  # extra pytest filters after --
./scripts/pytest_batches.sh --cov --domain-gate           # coverage + domain gate
FAIL_FAST=1 ./scripts/pytest_batches.sh                   # stop on first failure
```

A single directory/file via plain `uv run pytest tests/domain/runs/ -q` is fine — never the full tree.

## Targeted batch by changed area

| Changed area | Batch |
|--------------|-------|
| `cys_core/domain/runs/`, `domain/observability/`, `domain/catalog/` | `tests/domain` |
| `cys_core/application/` | `tests/application` |
| `cys_core/registry/`, `agents/` | `tests/registry` |
| `interfaces/api/` | `tests/api` |
| spawn / mode policy | `tests/adversarial` |
| catalog / run state infra | `tests/infrastructure` |

## Why

- Frees memory between `tests/<dir>/` batches (separate pytest processes).
- Avoids collection errors from module name collisions across batches.
- Matches CI and [AGENTS.md](projects/egregore/AGENTS.md) verify workflow.

## Env defaults

`USE_MEMORY_FALLBACK=true STAGE=test` — set automatically by the script.
